        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7dfa2d191ffb473ea0561af4359ad060",
      "statement": "login generates the keypair in memory, requests the CA Version, and when RequireClientAuthentication is set includes a CA-created x509 identity CSR in SSHSign and writes the returned identity certificate as the default identity; the signed certificate is added to the agent, and --add-user also creates and loads a second provisioner keypair/certificate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ssh/login.go#L203-L302",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8f0421439c726c224fa14be0521e79bfcf0c696da0a3091c05af0796c0a62473:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5514d3251d8546c5a8b146a0c0d1431c",
      "statement": "step ssh renew authenticates with an SSHPOP token: it sets sshpop-cert/sshpop-key from the existing certificate and key files and uses the certificate serial as the token subject before calling SSHRenew, writing the new certificate and renewed identity certificate back to disk.",
